[02:02:55.154] ======================================================================
[02:02:55.154] THE THREE CHAINS (README 九)
[02:02:55.154] ======================================================================
[02:02:55.154] 1) C var -> GCC -> ELF .text/.data/.bss -> ELF loader -> VMA
[02:02:55.154]    -> page table -> MMU -> physical RAM
[02:02:55.154] 2) malloc() -> glibc allocator -> brk/mmap -> demand paging
[02:02:55.154] 3) C pointer -> LOAD/STORE -> MMU -> page fault -> SIGSEGV on error
[02:02:55.154] Not every page fault is a bug: demand paging and COW are normal.
